.TH RAW2FITS 1 "November 2026" "raw2fits 1.0.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
raw2fits \- convert camera RAW files to FITS for astronomical stacking
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B raw2fits
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIRAW-FILE\fR...
.br
.B raw2fits-par
[\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR] [\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIRAW-FILE\fR...
.br
.B cafrun \-n
\fIN\fR
.B raw2fits-caf
[\fIOPTION\fR]... \fIRAW-FILE\fR...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B raw2fits
decodes camera RAW files with LibRaw and writes the unprocessed sensor data
as 16\-bit FITS images: no demosaicing, white balance or colour conversion.
The CFA (Bayer) pattern of the written area, exposure time, date, ISO,
temperature and camera/lens names are stored in the header, so the files
can be calibrated and stacked directly (e.g. in Siril or ASTAP).
.PP
Output files are written next to each RAW file (or into \fB\-\-outdir\fR)
with the RAW extension replaced: \fIIMG_0001.CR2\fR becomes
\fIIMG_0001.fits\fR. RAW files that store several channels produce one file
per channel (\fIIMG_0001.ch1.fits\fR, ...).
.PP
Files are converted in parallel by one of two backends. \fBraw2fits\fR uses
OpenMP threads: \fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR converts \fIN\fR files at a time (default: all
cores); the release packages use this backend. \fBraw2fits-caf\fR (built with
\fBmake BACKEND=coarray\fR) is the
Fortran coarray build. Started with \fBcafrun \-n\fR \fIN\fR,
it shares the input files between \fIN\fR images that convert in parallel.
\fBraw2fits-par\fR does this with one image per physical CPU core (or
\fB\-j\fR \fIN\fR). Use at least 2 images: with Debian/Ubuntu OpenMPI 4.1 a
coarray program aborts in MPI_Win_create when started as a single image.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-f\fR, \fB\-\-format\fR=\fIFMT\fR
\fBfits\fR (default), \fBtiff\fR (16\-bit TIFF with FITS cards in the
ImageDescription tag, "AstroTIFF") or \fBpgm\fR.
.TP
\fB\-a\fR, \fB\-\-area\fR=\fIAREA\fR
\fBactive\fR (default): visible sensor area; \fBfull\fR: whole sensor
including masked (optical black) pixels; \fBcrop\fR: the camera's default
crop, or the active area if the file has none.
.TP
\fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-outdir\fR=\fIDIR\fR
Write the output into \fIDIR\fR, which is created if necessary.
.TP
\fB\-e\fR, \fB\-\-keep\-ext\fR
Keep the RAW extension in the output name (\fIIMG_0001.CR2.fits\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-ext\fR=\fIEXT\fR
Use \fIEXT\fR as output extension, e.g. \fBfit\fR.
.TP
\fB\-S\fR, \fB\-\-skip\-existing\fR
Do not convert files whose output already exists (resume an interrupted run).
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
List the planned conversions without writing anything.
.TP
\fB\-s\fR, \fB\-\-shot\fR=\fIN\fR
Select the \fIN\fRth image of multi\-shot RAW files (default 0). For
\fIN\fR > 0, \fB\-\fR\fIN\fR is appended to the output name.
.TP
\fB\-l\fR, \fB\-\-list\fR=\fIFILE\fR
Read RAW file names from \fIFILE\fR, one per line; empty lines and lines
starting with \fB#\fR are ignored.
.TP
\fB\-A\fR, \fB\-\-autoscale\fR
Multiply low\-range data by an integer factor so they fill the 16\-bit range.
.TP
\fB\-g\fR, \fB\-\-gamma\fR
Apply gamma 2.2. For visual inspection only: the data are no longer linear.
.TP
\fB\-j\fR, \fB\-\-jobs\fR=\fIN\fR
Number of OpenMP threads converting files at the same time (default 0: all
cores, or \fBOMP_NUM_THREADS\fR). Ignored by \fBraw2fits-caf\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-schedule\fR=\fBstatic\fR|\fBdynamic\fR
Coarray build: how files are shared between images: \fBstatic\fR (default) gives
image \fIk\fR files \fIk\fR, \fIk+N\fR, ...; \fBdynamic\fR lets every image
take the next unconverted file.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Report errors only.
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Report sensor geometry and processing details for every file.
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Show a summary of the options.
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Show the program and LibRaw versions and the parallel backend.
.PP
Short options can be combined (\fB\-qS\fR) and take their value attached
(\fB\-ofits\fR) or as the next argument. \fB\-\-\fR ends the options.
.SH FITS HEADER
BITPIX = 16 with BZERO = 32768 (unsigned 16\-bit), ROWORDER = 'TOP\-DOWN',
BAYERPAT/FILT\-PAT and XBAYROFF/YBAYROFF = 0 for the written area, EXPTIME,
DATE\-OBS, JD, CCD\-TEMP, ISOSPEED, GAIN (= ISO), PEDESTAL* (black levels),
DATAMAX*, APERTURE, FOCALLEN, CAMMAKER, INSTRUME, TELESCOP (lens), IMG_FLIP,
RAWAREA, RAWX0, RAWY0 and SWCREATE.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 if all files were converted (or skipped), 1 if any file failed or was not
supported, 2 for usage errors.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
raw2fits *.CR2
raw2fits \-o fits/ \-a full ~/lights/*.NEF
raw2fits \-n \-o fits/ *.ARW          # what would be done?
raw2fits \-j 8 \-o fits/ *.NEF        # 8 threads
cafrun \-n 4 raw2fits-caf \-S \-o fits/ *.ARW
raw2fits-par \-j 8 \-o fits/ \-l lights.txt
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B OMP_NUM_THREADS
Default number of threads for \fBraw2fits\fR when \fB\-j\fR is not given.
.TP
.B RAW2FITS_JOBS
Default number of images for \fBraw2fits-par\fR.
.SH NOTES
DATE\-OBS is derived from the camera's timestamp and is correct UTC only if
the camera clock was set to the time zone of the converting computer.
Floating\-point DNG data are scaled linearly to 0..65535.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR cafrun (1),
.BR siril (1)
